      {
        "id": 0,
        "original_id": "7639a36d-226c-582c-8adf-40903f7b8fbf",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: James Fowle Baldwin, George Rumford Baldwin, Loammi Baldwin, Loammi Baldwin Jr., Cyrus Baldwin, Benjamin Franklin Baldwin\n- Projects: Middlesex Canal, Boston and Lowell Railroad, Boston and Albany Railroad, Boston, Hartford, and Erie Railroad, Buffalo and Mississippi Railroad, Lake Cochituate water supply\n- Companies: Boston and Maine Railroad\n- Places: Massachusetts, Boston, City of Quebec\n- Roles: Civil engineers\n\nFacts:\n- James Fowle Baldwin (April 29, 1782 – May 20, 1862) was an early American civil engineer.\n- George Rumford Baldwin was born in North Woburn on January 26, 1798 and died there on October 11, 1888.\n- James Fowle Baldwin worked with his father and brothers on the Middlesex Canal.\n- George Rumford Baldwin worked with his father Loammi Baldwin and his brothers Loammi Baldwin Jr., Cyrus Baldwin, Benjamin Franklin Baldwin, and James Fowle Baldwin on the Middlesex Canal and other projects.\n- James Fowle Baldwin surveyed and designed the Boston and Lowell Railroad and the Boston and Albany Railroad.\n- James Fowle Baldwin worked on Boston’s first water supply from Lake Cochituate and many other early engineering projects.\n- George Rumford Baldwin later surveyed and engineered the Boston, Hartford, and Erie Railroad, the Buffalo and Mississippi Railroad, and the gas and water systems for the City of Quebec.\n- The Boston and Lowell Railroad was a historic railroad that operated in Massachusetts in the United States.\n- The Boston and Lowell Railroad later operated as part of the Boston and Maine Railroad’s Southern Division.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
        "id": 1,
